      "writtenOn": "2025-07-24T16:38:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Continuing the discussion on the large number of hash collisions.\n\n`hash_value1` is the index to a slot (bucket) in the hash table. Should we incorporate the x and y coordinates of the intrabc candidate block into `hash_value1` to reduce the number of collisions?",
      "revId": "2bfb5a146134b657c9f0045f82508be497622582",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ccb9886_df61427f",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/hash_motion.c",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 289,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-24T16:51:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t believe we want to incorporate coordinates to the hash key `hash_value1`, because that\u0027d be counter-productive to finding matches from different regions of the image. For intraBC, we do want to group the same-looking candidates together into the same bucket by design.",
